---
import KnockioHomeLayout from "../../layouts/KnockioHomeLayout.astro";
import "../../styles/comparisons.css";

const title = "Knockio vs ServiceTitan (2026): Enterprise Power vs Same Day Simplicity";
const description = "A sourced comparison of Knockio and ServiceTitan. The enterprise standard against a platform built for small and midsize home service teams.";

const jsonLd = [
  {
    "@context": "https://schema.org",
    "@type": "BreadcrumbList",
    itemListElement: [
      { "@type": "ListItem", position: 1, name: "Home", item: "https://knockio.com/" },
      { "@type": "ListItem", position: 2, name: "Comparisons", item: "https://knockio.com/comparisons/" },
      { "@type": "ListItem", position: 3, name: "Knockio vs ServiceTitan", item: "https://knockio.com/comparisons/knockio-vs-servicetitan/" },
    ],
  },
  {
    "@context": "https://schema.org",
    "@type": "FAQPage",
    mainEntity: [
      {
        "@type": "Question",
        name: "Is ServiceTitan too expensive for a small business?",
        acceptedAnswer: { "@type": "Answer", text: "It is quote only and widely reported as high cost with minimums, as of July 2026, and the company says it is not optimized for shops with three or fewer technicians. Knockio publishes $20 to $60 per user per month for small and midsize teams." },
      },
      {
        "@type": "Question",
        name: "How long does ServiceTitan take to implement?",
        acceptedAnswer: { "@type": "Answer", text: "Reviews commonly report six to twelve months. Knockio is designed to run the same day." },
      },
      {
        "@type": "Question",
        name: "Does ServiceTitan have canvassing?",
        acceptedAnswer: { "@type": "Answer", text: "Not natively; it relies on third party integrations. Knockio includes canvassing, territories, and live rep tracking." },
      },
      {
        "@type": "Question",
        name: "Does Knockio replace ServiceTitan?",
        acceptedAnswer: { "@type": "Answer", text: "For large enterprises using its full depth, not necessarily. For small and midsize contractors it covers the core sales to invoice workflow at a fraction of the cost and setup time." },
      },
    ],
  },
];
---

<KnockioHomeLayout title={title} description={description} jsonLd={jsonLd}>
  <main>
    <section class="hero">
      <div class="wrap">
        <span class="kicker">Comparison</span>
        <h1>Knockio vs ServiceTitan</h1>
        <p class="lede">ServiceTitan is the enterprise standard for large trade operations, and it deserves that title at twenty or more technicians. It is also quote only, widely reported as expensive, and commonly takes six to twelve months to implement. <b>Knockio is built for the small and midsize teams it prices out: live the same day, at a published price, with canvassing built in.</b></p>
        <p class="byline">Last reviewed July 2026 &middot; Written by the Knockio team &middot; Every figure is sourced below</p>
        <div class="verdict">
          <h2>The short answer</h2>
          <p>Unless you run an enterprise sized operation, Knockio is the practical choice. ServiceTitan is the right call for large multi location operations with the budget and patience for a long rollout.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="choose">
          <div>
            <h3>Choose Knockio if</h3>
            <ul>
              <li>You run a small or midsize team, not an enterprise</li>
              <li>You want to be live the same day, not next year</li>
              <li>You want a published, predictable price</li>
              <li>You want door to door canvassing built in</li>
            </ul>
          </div>
          <div class="them">
            <h3>Choose ServiceTitan if</h3>
            <ul>
              <li>You run twenty or more technicians, or multiple locations</li>
              <li>You need enterprise reporting, purchasing, and inventory at scale</li>
              <li>You can absorb a long implementation and per technician pricing</li>
              <li>You will genuinely use the enterprise depth</li>
            </ul>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section>
      <div class="wrap">
        <h2>Side by side</h2>
        <p class="section-note">What each platform covers out of the box. Partial means the capability exists but is limited or costs extra.</p>
        <div class="table-scroll">
          <table>
            <thead>
              <tr><th>Capability</th><th class="c kn">Knockio</th><th class="c">ServiceTitan</th></tr>
            </thead>
            <tbody>
              <tr><td>Canvassing and door knocking</td><td class="c kn"><span class="yes">&#10003;</span></td><td class="c"><span class="no">&#10005;</span><span class="cell-note">Via third party tools</span></td></tr>
              <tr><td>Sales pipeline and CRM</td><td class="c kn"><span class="yes">&#10003;</span></td><td class="c"><span class="yes">&#10003;</span></td></tr>
              <tr><td>Estimates and proposals</td><td class="c kn"><span class="yes">&#10003;</span></td><td class="c"><span class="yes">&#10003;</span></td></tr>
              <tr><td>Crew and job scheduling</td><td class="c kn"><span class="yes">&#10003;</span></td><td class="c"><span class="yes">&#10003;</span></td></tr>
              <tr><td>Timesheets and time tracking</td><td class="c kn"><span class="yes">&#10003;</span></td><td class="c"><span class="yes">&#10003;</span></td></tr>
              <tr><td>Invoicing and payments</td><td class="c kn"><span class="yes">&#10003;</span></td><td class="c"><span class="yes">&#10003;</span></td></tr>
              <tr><td>Inventory and vendor bills</td><td class="c kn"><span class="yes">&#10003;</span></td><td class="c"><span class="yes">&#10003;</span></td></tr>
              <tr><td>Automations</td><td class="c kn"><span class="yes">&#10003;</span></td><td class="c"><span class="yes">&#10003;</span></td></tr>
              <tr><td>Map view of jobs</td><td class="c kn"><span class="yes">&#10003;</span></td><td class="c"><span class="partial">Partial</span><span class="cell-note">Map based dispatch</span></td></tr>
              <tr><td>Mobile app for field crews</td><td class="c kn"><span class="yes">&#10003;</span></td><td class="c"><span class="yes">&#10003;</span></td></tr>
            </tbody>
          </table>
        </div>
        <p class="table-foot">Verified from public sources as of July 2026. Sources at the end of this page.</p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section>
      <div class="wrap">
        <h2>Pricing</h2>
        <p class="section-note">Prices change. Confirm current figures on each vendor site before you buy.</p>
        <div class="price-grid">
          <div class="price-card kn">
            <h3>Knockio</h3>
            <p>$20 to $60 per user per month, published, with every feature included on every plan. As of July 2026, knockio.com.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="price-card">
            <h3>ServiceTitan</h3>
            <p>Not publicly disclosed. Quote only, per technician. Third party analyses report roughly $245 to $500 per technician per month plus an implementation fee and a twelve month minimum. As of July 2026.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="read">
      <div class="wrap">
        <h2>The honest read</h2>
        <h3>What ServiceTitan does well</h3>
        <ul>
          <li>The deepest feature set in the category, from dispatch to payroll</li>
          <li>Strong reporting and business analytics</li>
          <li>Robust call booking, scheduling, and dispatch</li>
          <li>Marketing attribution that ties ad spend to booked revenue</li>
        </ul>
        <h3>Where it can fall short</h3>
        <ul>
          <li>High and variable cost, with add ons that grow the bill</li>
          <li>Onboarding commonly runs six to twelve months</li>
          <li>Widely called overkill below about fifteen technicians</li>
          <li>Support speed and rigid contracts are frequent complaints</li>
        </ul>
        <h3>Why teams pick Knockio instead</h3>
        <p>This comparison is really about company size. ServiceTitan itself says the platform is not optimized for the smallest shops. <b>Most home service companies are exactly that size</b>, and for them the depth becomes weight: features they pay for and never open.</p>
        <p>Knockio takes the opposite bet: canvassing, CRM, scheduling, and invoicing running the same day at $20 to $60 per user per month, published. If you are big enough to use ServiceTitan properly, it earns its reputation. If you are not, you are its wrong customer, by its own admission.</p>
        <h3>What to know before choosing Knockio</h3>
        <p>Knockio is a newer platform, so its integration marketplace and review history are smaller than long established tools. The upside of newer is speed: published pricing, same day setup, and a product that ships quickly. Pressure test everything on a live demo rather than taking our word for it.</p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="faq">
      <div class="wrap">
        <h2>Common questions</h2>
        <details>
          <summary>Is ServiceTitan too expensive for a small business?</summary>
          <div class="answer">It is quote only and widely reported as high cost with minimums, as of July 2026, and the company says it is not optimized for shops with three or fewer technicians. Knockio publishes $20 to $60 per user per month for small and midsize teams.</div>
        </details>
        <details>
          <summary>How long does ServiceTitan take to implement?</summary>
          <div class="answer">Reviews commonly report six to twelve months. Knockio is designed to run the same day.</div>
        </details>
        <details>
          <summary>Does ServiceTitan have canvassing?</summary>
          <div class="answer">Not natively; it relies on third party integrations. Knockio includes canvassing, territories, and live rep tracking.</div>
        </details>
        <details>
          <summary>Does Knockio replace ServiceTitan?</summary>
          <div class="answer">For large enterprises using its full depth, not necessarily. For small and midsize contractors it covers the core sales to invoice workflow at a fraction of the cost and setup time.</div>
        </details>
      </div>
    </section>

    <div class="notes">
      <div class="wrap">
        <h2>How we compared these</h2>
        <p>This page is built from vendor pricing and product pages plus independent review sites such as G2 and Capterra. Where a vendor does not publish a figure we say so rather than estimate. Knockio publishes this page, so we have a stake in the outcome. That is exactly why we keep it honest, and why we name what ServiceTitan does well. Spot something out of date? Tell us and we will fix it.</p>
        <ul>
          <li><a href="https://www.servicetitan.com/pricing" rel="nofollow noopener" target="_blank">ServiceTitan pricing, request only</a>. Accessed July 2026.</li>
          <li><a href="https://www.servicetitan.com/features" rel="nofollow noopener" target="_blank">ServiceTitan features</a>. Accessed July 2026.</li>
          <li><a href="https://www.capterra.com/p/150053/ServiceTitan/" rel="nofollow noopener" target="_blank">ServiceTitan reviews, Capterra, 4.3 of 5 from about 336 reviews</a>. Accessed July 2026.</li>
          <li><a href="https://projul.com/blog/servicetitan-pricing-analysis-2026/" rel="nofollow noopener" target="_blank">ServiceTitan pricing analysis, Projul, third party estimate</a>. Accessed July 2026.</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </div>

    <section class="cta">
      <h2>See Knockio on your own workflow.</h2>
      <p>Twenty minutes, your real process, live on screen. Then decide with your own eyes.</p>
      <div class="cta-buttons">
        <a class="btn btn-green" href="https://knockio.com/book-a-demo/">Book a demo</a>
        <a class="btn btn-outline" href="https://knockio.com/pricing/">See pricing</a>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="related">
      <div class="wrap">
        <h2>More comparisons</h2>
        <div class="related-links">
          <a href="/comparisons/">All comparisons</a>
          <a href="/comparisons/knockio-vs-jobber/">Knockio vs Jobber</a>
          <a href="/comparisons/knockio-vs-spotio/">Knockio vs SPOTIO</a>
          <a href="/comparisons/knockio-vs-jobnimbus/">Knockio vs JobNimbus</a>
          <a href="/comparisons/knockio-vs-housecall-pro/">Knockio vs Housecall Pro</a>
          <a href="/comparisons/knockio-vs-fieldpulse/">Knockio vs FieldPulse</a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>
  </main>
</KnockioHomeLayout>
